  "sport": "bandy",
  "title": "Edges and balance for the youngest",
  "description": "The children line up along one end with the stick in one hand and the blade on the ice. Put two cones a little way out to mark where the strides end. The players take 4–6 quick strides up to the cones and then glide as far as they can. Skate back easily and do the next task:\n\n1) Glide on both skates, side by side. 2) Glide and sink down – knees forward, bottom down, straight back. 3) Glide and press first the right, then the left skate a little outwards so the edge bites, and bring it back. 4) Glide on one skate, switch legs next time. The last run is done with a ball in front of the stick.\n\nShort rounds and lots of praise. Break it up with a game. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Bend at the ankles, knees and hips – stay low."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Straight back and eyes forward, not down at the ice."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Stick in one hand with the blade on the ice."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "Falling is fine – get up and try again."
    }
  ],
